{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## 3. Research records\n\nP1 deep dive (three subagents). Implementation: overlap never ran at CREATE, only after plan-review certification; digests and queue coordination were persisted as events on the shared auto-pushed tickets branch; no persisted index, so each query re-reduced every ticket (about 48 s on this store); 105,197 of 147,074 event files (71.5 percent) were overlap sidecars; 93 percent of digests were recomputed for unchanged content; the drain gate rode every store write and spawned a detached interpreter. Reusable: the ticket_digest schema and prompt, the BM25F scorer, graph exclusion, the judge prompt and batch contract, the calibration data, the content-hash freshness idea, and recent_creates.py as the model for per-clone derived state. Ticket history: epic only-crave-art (bd83-c56f-1f72-4ef2), seven children landed 07-09/10, ADR 0086; embeddings were rejected on an eight-pair experiment; six bug clusters all trace to the architecture (prune outside the lock, prune breaking union-merge, unbounded growth and write storms, an O(store) gate on every write, an unbounded judge, detached-child hygiene); create-time was never wired; 44 of 51 real duplicate pairs are semantic not lexical; the 08-31 disable also disabled the same-title journal. OSS survey (git-bug, Fossil, jj, Cargo, Zoekt, Gitea, Zulip, Discourse, Bugzilla, GitLab, GitHub, Linear, Sentry): every comparable system keeps the index as a disposable, version-keyed local cache outside the replicated store, caught up in the reader's process, with compose-time similarity lexical-first and non-blocking and any model call off the write path. Synthesis: right retrieval pattern, wrong persistence and coordination architecture (ADR 0086 section 3, the event store as queue and cache). Recommended next shape: per-clone SQLite index keyed by tickets HEAD SHA and format version, catch-up in the reader, create-time query top 3 to 5 advisory, LLM judge on demand; the operator's framing is vector search over summaries (Amazon Titan Text Embeddings V2 identified as the candidate model). Recorded as the design-record epic fattish-plucky-bufflehead and its research story.\n\nP12 versus the janitor's RP08 rejection. RP08 rested on topaz-blubbery-mice (no generated adapters, Pattern A) and ruinable-cozey-caracal. The revisit bar was a post-oracle escape and it was met once: lowly-lawrencium-ovenbird (2026-09-02) found the MCP output mirror under-declared 41 schema properties. ADR 0100 section 2's non-derivable CLI cases stand. Verdict: reject P12 in full, stage P12 narrow for MCP only. Experiments later confirmed the FastMCP mechanism (a dict return gets a pass-through RootModel; setting fn_metadata.output_schema to an inlined canonical schema is advertised and validated; inlining is mandatory because jsonschema cannot resolve cross-file refs), measured the null-versus-absent wire delta (show_ticket 44 keys and 12 nulls on the wire versus 36 and 6 from the library) and enumerated eight input divergences for the override table.\n\nP13. The bridge runs _bridge_runner -> rebar bridge sync -> python -m rebar_reconciler; _lib_ops._bridge_run bypasses the guarded core so MCP bridge_sync runs an unlocked live pass; the outer 3600 s kill orphans the grandchild. Fix: one guarded core, direct spawn with start_new_session and process-group reaping, subprocess boundary kept.\n\nP17 residue confirmed dead on origin/main via Serena plus git grep: the _hash_basis(at_current_gate_ref=) branch, read_set.terraform_membership_entries, identical CLOSE and DRIFT_REFRESH profiles, a duplicated unresolvable-ref message, and the not-closed verdict unreachable from plan_review_status. _legacy_material_ok is live and kept.\n\nP19 verified: repo-root bridge_state/ snapshots, sync logs, alerts and the sync-route manifest have no retention; the snapshot is a same-pass round trip; a client at 1,000 issues hourly writes about 0.8 GB per day. Fix: keep-last-5 snapshots and sync logs, 30 alert days, prune in persist_and_log, move to .rebar/bridge/.\n\nHMAC. All 3,883 live SIGNATURE events on this tracker are Ed25519 op-certs; story 8f1d's contract phase already refuses the legacy scheme for both op-cert kinds; the HMAC module only verifies records nothing mints. Retiring it means non-envelope records read as unsigned with a retired-scheme reason; worst case is a re-review, never store breakage."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788839646349069001,"uuid":"e5e84225-7d8f-49f7-acfa-6082f5c2e229"}